{
 "_": "Brief 5 loot: which authored piece each opponent drops and the player slot it fills. Sources are parts.py/items outputs in the shared unscaled rest space (build-warrior.mjs contract: extras.material/slot + extras.bone or skin weights). `slots`/`names` pick meshes out of a shared file; `unscale` names the BUILD proportion table a piece was cut under. Slots: Helmet, Crest, Body, Arms, Gloves, Greaves, Boots. `layer`: 'replace' hides the player's own draws in that slot (a helm hides the hair, a tunic the tunic, boots the sandals); 'over' is worn on top of them (greaves over bare shins, a plate over a wrap). Body = the tunic and what hangs on it (baldric, belt, buckle, studs, collar) — kilt/skirt/hose are leg cloth with no paperdoll slot and stay the player's; wraps are the Arms item where an opponent wears nothing over them. A tunic's material becomes Gambeson_<opponent> (his own linen bake) — see build-warrior.mjs. A `replace` piece must cover at least 80 % of the player's own draws in that slot (tests/loot.test.ts): the Pitborn's chest is a rag sash at 26 % of the player's tunic, so it ships `over` (worn on top of the tunic, hiding nothing) rather than `replace`. `conform`: the piece was cut from another frame (a broader or a female sculpt); the build pushes it out along its normals until it clears the player's body and level-1 kit (scripts/loot-fit.mjs).",
 "~shared": {
  "_": "Brief 14: pieces the whole roster shares. A shared piece is EXPORTED ONCE, as `~<id>.<material>`; an opponent wears it with {\"slot\", \"layer\", \"shared\": \"<id>\"} and contributes no geometry of its own. The build writes the `<opponent>.<slot>` -> `~<id>` map into loot.glb's own scene userData, so the file is self-describing and a loader can resolve either schema. Loot always binds to the PLAYER's rig, so a shared piece needs exactly one fit here - the per-rig-family dimension only exists in the opponents' own fight GLBs.",
  "kit.Gloves": {
   "slot": "Gloves",
   "layer": "over",
   "file": "@build:gloves"
  },
  "kit.Shield": {
   "slot": "Shield",
   "layer": "over",
   "file": "@build:shield"
  }
 },
